Greetings, brave explorers of Nanraas! Winter is almost over, and the nature is finally starting to wake up. Thus, another natural cycle keeps on rolling, so we have to get prepared for more sun and warmth. Cold and dull weather usually makes feel a bit ill, antsy and drained of energy, but the upcoming spring should fix our mood and pace of life. Despite being under the weather, our team has been working hard to bring you the top-notch freshly baked content and long-awaited updated. So, let’s cut to the chase!

We keep on working hard every day to make your gaming experience on release as smooth as possible. Unfortunately, the wintertime and some events in Ukraine slowed down our progress, so we decided to postpone the release date of the game in order not to turn a blind eye on potential bugs, glitches, inconsistencies, and presence of certain outdated pieces of content in HotA. But worry not! We’re releasing the game this spring! However, the release date itself has been moved to May (wait for the announce). By the way, according to the lore, Azaries’ adventures actually happened in spring, so let’s start this wonderful journey together with our bellowed om’verai!

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/43833712/8c66c81601c80c8180da30d4b2f2c2c559a70554.jpg[/img]

Thus, long ours of hardcore coding, drawing, and translating have resulted into the following list of achievements:

· We’ve finally completed the revision of the first in-game days, which resulted in reworked animations, improved logic of the cutscenes, implementation of the newly designed animations/reactions of certain characters as well as revamped backgrounds and even more minor cosmetic changes;

· We’ve revised and updated Ukrainian (VA+text) and English (Text) localizations of the game.

· The differences between Azaries’ classes have been further deepened and substantiated. The new Stats Check System (SCS) opens a wide variety of ways to customize MC’s behavior and unlocks multiple choices/branches during the events of main story, as well as adds unique class- and architype-exclusive events/quests/ways to act under certain circumstances;

·  Ukrainian VO for all characters encountered in High Circles is currently in production (the EA release will feature full VO of Prologue and High Circles (beginning of Chapter One), except for optional dialogs and side stories);

· Combat system has been heavily rebalanced. We’ve revised and discussed stats of the majority of enemies encountered in order to enhance the combat experience depending on the difficulty level selected;

· UI has been improved and updated;

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/43833712/ed49b30231c82ab151c211f727a2fd82b3d13f69.png[/img]

Our plans for March/to do list:

· To completely revise few days of Azaries’ journey in order to implement the same set of improvements/animations/cutscenes to meet our new standards of in-game storytelling logic;

· To finish the development of the secondary in-game modules, such as «Dictionary», «Jukebox crystal» and«Memories». Each modules will provide the player with certain non-essential in-game mechanics. For example, the «Dictionary» module will allow to read all the collected info regarding om’veri language, terms, definitions and meaning of certain words and even the deciphered fragments of the ancient tongue. Also, System of Azaries’ flashbacks, which is currently in developments, will unlock and save all viewed memory fragments regardless of the current save state and route chosen. Basically, each player will be able to watch each encountered and viewed/skipped flashback again in main menu or in-game even if they start a new playthrough or delete the save folder. This system proves useful for returning players and those who admire collecting the pieces of lore and story together. However, the memories must be collecting first by progressing the main plot or meeting certain requirements;

· To fully revise/finish/polish Ukrainian and English localizations of currently existing content.

· To rework/improve/enhance UI/graphics in certain game situations;

· More fixes, improvements, and optimizations of all aspects of the game!

Also, a few weeks before the release we will remove the playable demo from Steam due to the urgent need to update it with newly polished content and remove certain inconsistencies. Updated Demo will be available in summer.

Thank you for your support! See you in Nanraas!

Greetings, heroes of Nanraas! We’ve been working really hard to bring this moment closer. And finally, we can proudly announce the release date of the playable demo of the Heralds of the Avirentes Ch.1 Wings of Change – Jul 11, 2023! We’ve been doing our best to make it possible and it finally happened! Hurray! In less than in a week everyone will be able to join Azaries on her adventures around Nanraas!
This playable demo features the following content:
•	Up to 7* hours of solid gameplay which includes full Prologue and the beginning of Chapter 1;
•	Full Ukrainian localization (including voice over (VO)**);
•	Three playable classes of the main character Azaries – you can try them all to choose the most suitable one***;
•	Branching dialogs with multiple options which impact the story, main character and the world around;
•	Substories and many character to interact with;
•	Advanced combat system and much more!
* Each playthrough is unique and depends on the player and their preferences. 7 hours is the average duration of a playthrough which involves reading all the dialogs and exploring all possible in-game events, their variations and class-exclusive dialog branches.
** Full Ukrainian voice over (VO) and voice acting (VA) extends to all main aspects of the game. However, some minor substories and/or interactions with NPCs may feature text only localization.
*** All three classes are available to the main character without specific requirement and prerequisites. However, once chosen, the class cannot be changed throughout the game. Each class features class-exclusive dialogs, events and substories.
Our game features full Ukrainian VO by team Melvoice! We hope you’ll enjoy amazing professional voice acting!
Thank you so much for your support! See you in Nanraas!
